Date: Fri, 26 Jun 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] mips: ingenic: drain bridge after DMA cache sync

Vendor XBurst kernels enable MIPS_BRIDGE_SYNC_WAR for Ingenic SoCs and
finish S-cache DMA maintenance with an uncached read through __fast_iob().
That read drains the external bridge/writeback buffer; a CPU sync alone is
not enough on affected systems.

Do the same after the generic Ingenic DMA writeback/invalidate helper and
after the XBurst DMA_FROM_DEVICE invalidate helper.  The former covers
TX-style paths and explicit writeback/invalidate users, while the latter is
the normal RX path used by DMA_FROM_DEVICE unmap/sync.

Without this patch, SFC DMA suffers from a race condition during a batch of small transfers
where the visible result is the result of one of previous operations, either fully or a glitched 32b chunk is injected in the middle.

The fact that kernel very quickly reuses allocations during MTD reads and operations very often start with the same DMA address, makes this 
race condition more visible.

Note: original author also added a specific code path for XBurst1 where the normal ingenic_blast_scache() is replaced with C0 ERRCTL manipulation.
That mechanic cannot be mapped anywhere to the vendor kernel or programming manual, nor was any documentation left on the reasoning.

No corruption is observed anymore, but if it reappears reverting that ERRCTL code path would be a reasonable thing to do.
---
 arch/mips/mm/c-ingenic.c | 5 +++++
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+)

diff --git a/arch/mips/mm/c-ingenic.c b/arch/mips/mm/c-ingenic.c
index 000000000000..111111111111 100644
--- a/arch/mips/mm/c-ingenic.c
+++ b/arch/mips/mm/c-ingenic.c
@@ -12,6 +12,7 @@
 #include <linux/sched.h>
 #include <linux/smp.h>
 
+#include <asm/barrier.h>
 #include <asm/bootinfo.h>
 #include <asm/cache.h>
 #include <asm/cacheops.h>
@@ -217,6 +218,8 @@ static void ingenic_dma_cache_wback_inv(unsigned long addr, unsigned long size)
 	preempt_enable();
 
 	__sync();
+	/* Match the vendor MIPS_BRIDGE_SYNC_WAR after DMA cache maintenance. */
+	__fast_iob();
 }
 
 static void ingenic_xburst_dma_cache_inv(unsigned long addr, unsigned long size)
@@ -233,6 +236,8 @@ static void ingenic_xburst_dma_cache_inv(unsigned long addr, unsigned long size)
 	preempt_enable();
 
 	__sync();
+	/* Match the vendor MIPS_BRIDGE_SYNC_WAR after DMA cache maintenance. */
+	__fast_iob();
 }
 
 static void ingenic_xburst2_dma_cache_inv(unsigned long addr, unsigned long size)
-- 
2.50.0

